      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the roots of $f(t)=\\frac{3t-9}{{t}^{2}+t-12}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The roots of $f(t)$ are the solutions to the equation $f(t)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{3t-9}{{t}^{2}+t-12}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\frac{3t-9}{{t}^{2}+t-12} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(t-3)}{(t-3)(t+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cancel{(t-3)}}{\\cancel{(t-3)}(t+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{t+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the numerator equal to zero, we get $3=0,$ which is a false statement. Therefore, $f(t)=0$ has no solution, and so $f(t)$ has no roots.",
