      "problem": "Solve $g(y)=0$ where $g(y)=\\frac{{y}^{3}-2{y}^{2}-25y+50}{{y}^{3}+{y}^{2}-25y-25}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y) & =\\frac{{y}^{3}-2{y}^{2}-25y+50}{{y}^{3}+{y}^{2}-25y-25} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}(y-2)-25(y-2)}{{y}^{2}(y+1)-25(y+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(y-2)({y}^{2}-25)}{(y+1)({y}^{2}-25)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(y-2)(y-5)(y+5)}{(y+1)(y-5)(y+5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(y-2)\\cancel{(y-5)(y+5)}}{(y+1)\\cancel{(y-5)(y+5)}} &  \\\\  & =\\frac{y-2}{y+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-2=0\\,⟹\\,y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $g(y)=0$ is $y=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
